    "raw": "First, let's determine the price of one kilogram of tomatoes. Given that one kilogram of cucumbers costs $5 and tomatoes are 20% cheaper, we can calculate the price of tomatoes as follows:\n\n\\[ \\text{Price of tomatoes per kg} = \\text{Price of cucumbers per kg} \\times (1 - 0.20) \\]\n\\[ \\text{Price of tomatoes per kg} = 5 \\times 0.80 = 4 \\]\n\nNext, we need to find the total cost for two kilograms of tomatoes and three kilograms of cucumbers:\n\n\\[ \\text{Total cost} = (2 \\times \\text{Price of tomatoes per kg}) + (3 \\times \\text{Price of cucumbers per kg}) \\]\n\\[ \\text{Total cost} = (2 \\times 4) + (3 \\times 5) \\]\n\\[ \\text{Total cost} = 8 + 15 = 23 \\]\n\nTherefore, the total cost for two kilograms of tomatoes and three kilograms of cucumbers is $23.\n\nFINAL: 23",
